  "actualEvidenceFindings": [
    "The explicit field contracts require TravelStatus, MessageRole and ChatMessageKind. Retaining all three is consistent with the detailed contract despite the card overview counting two enums.",
    "Database XOR, lowercase SHA-256 format, nonnegative version, positive sequence, composite unique indexes and foreign-key delete rules are implemented by the actual additive SQL. Both previous migration byte hashes remain unchanged.",
    "Owner-sensitive operations lock and recheck the owned record in the same transaction. Retry comparison includes role, kind, content, contentJson and reply target while replaying stored server-assigned fields. Cursor validation binds record, sequence, id and a persisted anchor.",
    "Real test evidence includes concurrency and ownership-change-after-lock cases, negative foreign-key and cross-record reply cases, rollback without subsequent writes, exact-ID fixture cleanup and preservation of other fixture records.",
    "Each SQL mutation file is byte-for-byte the final migration with only its designated owner CHECK or one composite unique index removed. Each targeted original rejects assertion failed because the promise resolved; restored targets passed and the complete 86-test card run has no failed, pending or todo tests.",
    "Final full Vitest contains 278 passing assertions with no failures, pending or todo tests; legacy User regression contains 31 and config/public-user results contain 44. All 18 quality command observations have exitCode zero and timedOut false.",
